WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.300
This is Creator Studio.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.220
It finds the best moments in your streams,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.710
and turns them into ready-to-post shorts.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.230
Let's set it up, then make your first clip.

5
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.670
First, install it.

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.720
Download the Creator Studio setup file, and run it.

7
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.230
You'll also need Python,

8
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.480
version 3.10 or newer.

9
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.100
When you install Python, tick: Add python to PATH.

10
00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.840
The first launch sets everything up by itself.

11
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.540
It takes a few minutes, and it only happens once.

12
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.160
The app has four tabs:

13
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.270
Clip downloader, Twitch clips,

14
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.470
ClipForge, and My shorts.

15
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.760
Start in the Clip downloader.

16
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.090
Scroll down to Find moments with Gemini.

17
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.080
This is the YouTube analyzer,

18
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.310
and it needs a free Gemini key.

19
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.550
Click the link to Google AI Studio,

20
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.670
create a key, and copy it.

21
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.580
Paste it here, and press Connect.

22
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.460
When the badge turns green,

23
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.280
Gemini is ready.

24
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.190
Next, open ClipForge.

25
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.890
In the top right, click AI director.

26
00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.490
With a free Coarena key,

27
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.490
the AI reads your clip and follows your instructions.

28
00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.680
Click: Get a free Coarena key.

29
00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.240
Copy it, paste it in, and press Save.

30
00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.220
The badge now says free. And that's the whole setup.

31
00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:16.830
Now let's make a clip.

32
00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.790
Copy the link to your stream VOD on YouTube,

33
00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.850
and paste it at the top of the Clip downloader.

34
00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:24.110
In the Gemini section,

35
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.540
choose Best moments or Funniest moments,

36
00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.840
pick how many, and add extra instructions if you want.

37
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.950
Then press Analyze video.

38
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.450
Gemini watches the stream, and gives you a list of moments,

39
00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.730
each with its time stamps,

40
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.560
a score, and why it works.

41
00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.610
Hit Download on the one you like.

42
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:43.260
You can also preview it, or adjust the times first.

43
00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.070
Got a Twitch clip instead?

44
00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.800
Open the Twitch clips tab, and paste the clip link.

45
00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.300
It downloads right away, in the best quality.

46
00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.530
Then press Edit in ClipForge.

47
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.030
In ClipForge, every clip you download shows up

48
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.080
under Downloaded clips. Click one to load it.

49
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.180
Now tell the AI what you want.

50
00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.220
Type it in plain words, or tap a quick idea, like Hook first.

51
00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.010
If a part must stay in,

52
00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.180
add a must-show moment, with its start and end time.

53
00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.640
Then pick the layout that fits your video.

54
00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.230
Full frame, with face follow,

55
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.700
is for podcasts and talking videos.

56
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.880
The crop glides smoothly to keep the speaker in the middle.

57
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.920
Split, reaction cam plus gameplay, is for gaming streamers.

58
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.640
The facecam goes on top, and the gameplay below.

59
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.050
It finds the facecam by itself,

60
00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.720
and you can drag the boxes to fix it.

61
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.760
Meme frame is for funny clips.

62
00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.430
Add a title on top and your handle,

63
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.700
and it looks like a classic meme post.

64
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.430
Turn on Heavy edit for punch-in zooms,

65
00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.420
shakes, flashes, circles,

66
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.390
arrows and emoji pops.

67
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.190
Below that, choose the format,

68
00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.850
how tightly to cut the pauses,

69
00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:48.690
where the captions go,

70
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.380
and the caption font. You can even drop in background music.

71
00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.320
It ducks under the voice automatically.

72
00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.940
When you're happy, press Edit my video.

73
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.010
Your finished shorts land in My shorts.

74
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.710
Download them, or delete the ones you don't need.

75
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.850
Press the pencil button, and the AI writes a caption,

76
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.030
a description with hashtags, and the best time to post.

77
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.270
Each one has its own copy button.

78
00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.460
A few more things.

79
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.370
If a video is age-restricted or members-only,

80
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.890
turn on YouTube sign-in with a cookies file.

81
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.040
The version badge at the top shows if you're up

82
00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.230
to date, and the app updates itself.

83
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.080
If you get stuck, click Join our community for

84
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.680
tutorials and help.

85
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:30.380
That's it.

86
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.200
Go make your first short.
